# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jonas Hänseroth et al. (2025). Optimizing machine learning interatomic potentials for hydroxide transport: Surprising efficiency of single-concentration training.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0284063  arXiv:2505.07580v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.07580v1 (sha256 b43088186844f388...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 301 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/hanseroth2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: MACE-MP-0 (small) fine-tuned on BLYP-D3 AIMD frames of
# aqueous KOH: 2,000-frame models at six concentrations (333 K), 200-frame
# models at four concentrations and four temperatures, and combined or
# multi-head models (A1, A2, B1-B3); force and energy RMSEs against AIMD
# at the training concentration (Table I), across concentrations (Table
# S2) and for the combined models (Fig. 4). Diffusion coefficients and
# structural analyses are properties, not error metrics.

