# - Errors are computed against AIMD reference data of each concentration and temperature; whether these frames are held out from training is not stated, so the roles are unset (the foundation model is external). Fig. 4 force RMSEs are read from the heat-map numbers (single-concentration columns match Table S2). Off-diagonal energy RMSEs in Table S2 are large (up to 4.3e4 meV/atom), reflecting energy offsets between concentrations as given.
# - Table S3 (temperature transfer) has inconsistent column headers and values that differ from Table I (e.g. 38.3 vs 38.9 meV/A for 0.56 mol/L at 303 K); it is not encoded. The 333 K 200-frame models are not listed in Table I.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/hanseroth2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

